  "prompt": "Stylised fantasy terrain map seen strictly from directly above - a flat 2D map view, no perspective, no horizon, no sky. Bold flat graphic shapes with crisp angular edges, like layered cut paper. Clean crisp edges, no outlines, no texture. Upper-left light. Tall portrait format. The whole land lies under a blood moon at night: the palette is deep maroon, plum and dusky violet ground, dark crimson-black forest masses, pale rose moonlit clearings, and one glowing pale teal pool.\n\nEverything is flat colour. Forests are flat dark plum-maroon masses speckled with tiny conifer and round tree shapes. Clearings are flat dusky rose fields with only the softest wash. No painterly brushwork, no relief shading, no light-and-shadow modelling of ground, no photographic terrain.\n\nA dense dark forest frames the image on all sides. Three moonlit clearings sit one above another down the middle of the image, joined by a thin pale winding trail with small dots of warm red lantern light along it. Each clearing is flat dusky rose-violet grass.\n\nLowest clearing, centred at 45 percent across and 78 percent down: a rabbit warren - dozens of small round dark burrow holes, each with a little crescent mound of pale earth, and a cluster of huge flat twisted tree roots spreading over one big burrow mouth.\n\nMiddle clearing, centred at 55 percent across and 50 percent down: a wide round glowing pale teal lake ringed by dark reeds, with a few flat drowned willow trees standing in its far side.\n\nHighest clearing, centred at 45 percent across and 22 percent down: a ring of flat grey standing stones on a low round mound, walled by tangled dark bramble thickets.\n\nNegative: no perspective view, no horizon, no sky, no moon drawn in the sky, no 3D render, no photorealism, no painterly rendering, no airbrush, no relief shading, no realistic landscape illustration, no aerial photograph, no text, no labels, no icons, no buildings, no castles, no characters, no map markers, no pins, n